From: vmapp <vmapp@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] ui: index.html without the inline script, loading the two vmapp scripts first

index.html carries the page's wiring to the native webview in one inline <script> (file picker callbacks, key and mouse guards,
drag-and-drop guards, the context-menu bridge). A vmapp window runs under the Content-Security-Policy `script-src 'self'`, which refuses
inline scripts, so the block moves to a file: apps/ollama-desktop/shim/ollama-desktop-shim.js has every line of it, rebuilt on window.vmapp
(PATCHES.md lists what became what). The second script is vmapp-fetch.js (sdk/web), which carries the page's `fetch('/api/...')` to the
backend over the bridge. Both are loaded first and are not bundled; build.sh copies them into the build output next to index.html.

